# FishBottle7/opencode2dsh PR #23 — https://github.com/FishBottle7/opencode2dsh/pull/23
# "fix(dsh-017): move the client onto configForms so the plugin activates on 0.1.7"
#
# DSH 0.1.7 removed the client-side `settingsScope` service and the keyed
# `settings.plugin.item` slot; the plugin still listed both as fiber
# dependencies, so the web UI parked it at
#   pending (waiting for service: settingsScope)
# and the whole plugin (settings card included) never activated. The PR moves
# the browser half onto the 0.1.7 contracts: `configForms` + the `plugins.item`
# list slot owned by the plugin-manager, the `Config` export with a volatile
# `ipPool` node in place of `ctx.settings.register()`, and
# `dsh.client.inject` package-row tokens. It also bumps the workspace
# dependencies — schemastery ^3.18.4 is REQUIRED at runtime
# (`IpPoolConfigSchema.volatile()` does not exist in 3.18.1) — so the pnpm
# lockfile changes and the derivation's pnpmDeps fixed-output hash is
# overridden alongside this patch (see dsh.nix).
#
# This copy is regenerated against the v0.3.2 tag that nur-DataEraserC pins
# (the PR targets master at package.json 0.3.3; of the files it touches only
# the package.json version line differs from v0.3.2), with paths rewritten
# relative to the package's sourceRoot = source/packages/plugin.
# Deliberately NOT part of this patch: docs (README*, docs/ip-pool.md,
# CHANGELOG.md) and test/* — they do not affect the build, and the 0.3.3-era
# test/README contexts no longer match v0.3.2. Drop this override once
# nur-DataEraserC ships a release containing the fix.
